<worksheet>
<title>Phase portraits for linear systems with Complex  eigenvalues</title>
<objectives>
<ul>
            <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with a Complex eigenvalue with a positive real part.</li>
            
                <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with a Complex eigenvalue with a negative real part.</li>
                    <li>
                        
                            Phase portraits for linear systems with a Complex eigenvalue with a zero real part.
                        
                    </li>
        </ul>    
</objectives>
<introduction>
    <p>
        In this worksheet we will discuss the cases of the phase portraits for the linear
                system
                <md>
                    \frac{d\vec{Y}}{dt}=A\vec{Y}
                </md>
                where <m>A</m> is a <m>2\times 2</m> matrix over <m>\mathbb{R}</m>, where the eigenvalues of <m>A</m> are complex, i.e. <m>\lambda=\alpha\pm\beta i</m>.
    </p>
</introduction>

<section>
    <title>Case 1: Spiral Source (<m>\alpha &gt; 0</m>)</title>
    <p>
        In this case, the phase portrait is a spiral source. The trajectories spiral outwards from the origin.
    </p>
    <example>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    For the system
                    <md alignment="align">
                                            <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt}&amp;=&amp;6x-y</mrow>
                                            <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt}&amp;=&amp;5x+4y</mrow>
                                        </md>
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task workspace="0.1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1, \lambda_2</m> of <m>A</m> and their corresponding eigenvectors <m>\vec{V_1}, \vec{V_2}</m>. 
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
           
           

            <task workspace="1.5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Expand the general solution <m>\vec{Y}(t)</m> in the form
                             <md>
                            \vec{Y}(t)=c_{1}\mbox{Re}\vec{Y(t)}+c_{2}\mbox{Im}\vec{Y(t)}.
                                                </md>   
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the solution with initial condition <m>\vec{Y}(0)=(0,-1)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Plot the phase portrait (<m>x(t)</m> vs <m>y(t)</m>)  and also plot <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </example>
    </section>

<section>
    <title>Case 2: Spiral Sink (<m>\alpha &lt; 0 </m>)</title>
    <p>
        In this case, the phase portrait is a spiral sink. The trajectories spiral inwards towards the origin.
    </p>
    <exercise>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    For the system
                    <md alignment="align">
                                            <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt}&amp;=&amp;-x+2y</mrow>
                                            <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt}&amp;=&amp;-x-3y</mrow>
                                        </md>
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task workspace="0.1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1, \lambda_2</m> of <m>A</m> and their corresponding eigenvectors <m>\vec{V_1}, \vec{V_2}</m>. 
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
           
           

            <task workspace="1.5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Expand the general solution <m>\vec{Y}(t)</m> in the form
                                                <md>
                                                    \vec{Y}(t)=c_{1}\mbox{Re}\vec{Y(t)}+c_{2}\mbox{Im}\vec{Y(t)}.
                                                </md>   
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the solution with initial condition <m>\vec{Y}(0)=(25,-10)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Plot the phase portrait (<m>x(t)</m> vs <m>y(t)</m>)  and also plot <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </exercise>

    </section>


<section>
<title>Case 3: Center (<m>\alpha = 0</m>)</title>
    <p>
        In this case, the phase portrait is a center. The trajectories are closed orbits around the origin.
    </p>

    <exercise>
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    For the system
                    <md alignment="align">
                                            <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt}&amp;=&amp;2x-4y</mrow>
                                            <mrow>\frac{dy}{dt}&amp;=&amp;2x-2y</mrow>
                                        </md>
                </p>
            </introduction>
 <task workspace="0.1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1, \lambda_2</m> of <m>A</m> and their corresponding eigenvectors <m>\vec{V_1}, \vec{V_2}</m>. 
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
<task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the solution with initial condition <m>\vec{Y}(0)=(20,20)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

<task workspace="1.5in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Expand the general solution <m>\vec{Y}(t)</m> in the form
                                                <md>
                                                    \vec{Y}(t)=c_{1}\mbox{Re}\vec{Y(t)}+c_{2}\mbox{Im}\vec{Y(t)}.
                                                </md>   
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            
            <task workspace="1.0in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Plot the phase portrait (<m>x(t)</m> vs <m>y(t)</m>)  and also plot <m>x(t)</m> and <m>y(t)</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            </exercise>
    </section>
</worksheet>


